#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Verify and fix metadata for a music library laid out as
<root>/<artist>/<album>/<song>.<ext>.

Artist/album are trusted from the folder structure; title and track
number come from a MusicBrainz text search, matched to the filename by
track number or (failing that) fuzzy title. The recording's full
artist credit (main + featured) goes to a separate "artists" tag --
the folder-trusted "artist" tag is left alone.

Pipeline, each step its own subcommand:

    scan <root> [queue]         Search MusicBrainz; queue metadata changes and
                                fresh album art for review.
    check [queue]               Sanity-check a queued changes file, prompting
                                for how to resolve anything suspicious.
    fingerprint <root> [queue]  AcoustID sanity check: does each queued title
                                roughly match the audio? Prints mismatches, no
                                prompts.
    apply <root> [queue]        Write a queued changes file's metadata and
                                album art to disk.
    normalize <root>            Loudness-normalize every track to a consistent
                                volume.
    convert <root> <from> <to>  Re-encode files from one format to another,
                                preserving metadata.
    rename <root> <format>      Rename files from a tag-rendered template.

[queue] defaults to tmp/changes.yml. scan never writes directly --
changes are queued to YAML for review, optionally sanity-checked with
check/fingerprint, then written with apply. Working files (queue,
queued art, backups) live in "tmp" next to wherever the script runs,
NOT inside root -- so scan stamps the queue with root's absolute path,
and apply refuses to run against a different root.

apply/normalize/convert/rename back root up to tmp/backups first,
unless --no-backup is given.

A ".mmfignore" file in root (".gitignore" syntax) excludes matching
files/folders from every step, including backups.

Setup:
    pip install mutagen pyacoustid musicbrainzngs pyyaml pillow pathspec
    # provides `fpcalc`, used by pyacoustid (needed for `fingerprint`):
    sudo apt install libchromaprint-tools
    # needed for `normalize` and `convert`:
    sudo apt install ffmpeg

    # Get a free AcoustID API key (no cost, just a signup), needed for
    # `fingerprint`:
    # https://acoustid.org/new-application
    export MMF_ACOUSTID_API_KEY=your_key_here

Usage:
    music_metafix scan /path/to/music/root
    music_metafix scan /path/to/music/root --no-art
    music_metafix scan /path/to/music/root custom-queue.yml
    music_metafix check
    music_metafix fingerprint /path/to/music/root
    music_metafix apply /path/to/music/root
    music_metafix apply /path/to/music/root custom-queue.yml
    music_metafix normalize /path/to/music/root
    music_metafix convert /path/to/music/root wma mp3
    music_metafix rename /path/to/music/root "%num - %title"
    music_metafix rename /path/to/music/root "%num - %title (feat. %features)"

A queue file's entries are paths relative to the root it was scanned
from, so `fingerprint`/`apply` need that same root.
"""

